  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.4.2 — Thread-safe streaming capture (fixes a response-corruption hazard in 0.4.1). Streaming (text/event-stream) usage is now captured via a non-blocking pass-through tee: the caller reads every byte itself while the SDK mirrors only the tail. The previous release read the response body on a background thread after handing the response to the caller, which could race and corrupt a streaming caller's response. Non-streaming capture now takes an owned buffered copy before returning. Also: Anthropic streaming input+output tokens are merged across SSE chunks; queue/worker resource-leak and clamp fixes. No code changes required.",
